# Act 3, chapter 7 "Activation" (Future Trunks's timeline, Age 767). Flags 330 chapter opened, 331 Gero killed,
# 332 outside (chapter end). Party: Seventeen = character 1 (form 14, actor 102), Eighteen = character 3 (form 23, actor 262).
# ch7_start runs straight on from the conversion scene (act2_siblings.scene) in the tank room 1:79.
list ch7_start
set_flag 330
say gero Rest while you can. Your first tests begin tomorrow.
narrate The tests did not go the way Dr. Gero planned.
narrate Seventeen ignored his orders. Eighteen laughed at them. Within a month he gave up, shut them both down and sealed them in their pods.
do call 120 60
do call 183 516 1462 1463
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1
do call 120 1; call 119 1 80 1 216 216; call 121 60
narrate Age 767. Dr. Gero's hidden laboratory.
narrate Son Goku is dead. A heart virus took him, not a fight. Gero's revenge was stolen from him.
say gero Goku is dead, and the two of you are all I have left. Wake up.
say android17 ...How long were we out?
say gero Long enough for the world to forget you. This time you will obey me, or I will shut you down for good.
say android18 That little box in your hand. That's the off switch, isn't it?
say gero Give me a reason to use it.
say android17 Here's one.
narrate Seventeen moved faster than the old man's thumb.
do call 120 30
set_flag 331
do call 119 1 81 1 216 216; call 121 60
say android18 ...That's it? He's just gone?
say android17 We're free, Eighteen. Nobody gets to tell us what to do. Not ever again.
narrate Far to the north, a machine Gero built years ago lost its creator's signal.
narrate Computer: Creator signal lost. Directive: destroy Son Goku. Target deceased. Contingency: complete Units Thirteen, Fourteen and Fifteen.
say android18 Did you hear something?
say android17 Just this place falling apart. Come on. I want to see the sky.
journal Leave Dr. Gero's hidden laboratory
do call 47; call 51 0
list eighteen_lab_talk
say android18 Don't look at me like that. I'm coming. I just wanted one more look at the pods.
# walk-in trigger at the arrival point of the Northern Wilderness 1:83 (flag 332 clear)
list ch7_end
set_flag 332
say android18 So this is outside. I'd forgotten how big it is.
say android17 Big and boring. Let's find a city and see what it's got.
say android18 Seventeen... do you remember the last city we were in?
say android17 Not really. Does it matter?
say android18 ...No. I guess it doesn't.
narrate End of Chapter 7.
run ch8_start
# ---------- the lab's lockdown (areas from log4/gen_ch7.py; flags 338 alarm, 339 Security Unit destroyed, 329 locker)
list ch7_alarm
set_flag 338
narrate Red lights. A siren, then the computer's flat voice from every speaker at once.
narrate Computer: Creator signal lost. Unregistered units in the laboratory. Lockdown. Security, purge the intruders.
say android17 Unregistered? He built us.
say android18 And now his house wants us dead. Charming.
say android17 There's a control room past this wing. We switch it off, we walk out the front door.
journal Get through the lockdown to the {c07}control room{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch7_locker
if_flag 329 locker_empty
set_flag 329
narrate Gero's workbench. Notes on Unit 16, a cold cup of tea... and a Senzu Bean in a labelled jar: "FOR EMERGENCIES".
say android18 He kept one for himself. Of course he did.
do call 129 11 1; call 129 1 1
stop
label locker_empty
narrate Gero's notes. Nothing worth reading.
list ch7_console
unless_flag 339 console_locked
narrate The security console. Seventeen finds the lockdown switch on the second try.
narrate Computer: Lockdown released. ...Continuing construction. Unit Thirteen: two percent. Fourteen: one percent. Fifteen: one percent.
say android18 More of us?
say android17 Not our problem. Let the old man's computer play with its toys.
say android18 Seventeen. If it finishes them, they'll come looking for us.
say android17 Then we'll be somewhere fun when they do. Come on.
narrate The hangar door grinds open. Cold mountain air pours in.
do call 120 30
do call 120 1; call 119 1 82 1 112 200; call 121 40
stop
label console_locked
narrate The console is behind the security machine. It isn't going to let anyone near it.
